{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 4.363, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 8090}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 8090, "cache_read_input_tokens": 3113, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 550, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_016RpGhDgqiPpdqTG6dYcLxn", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "LEP2 condition: for the Higgs-strahlung process e+e- → Z h, the SM 114.4 GeV bound is recast as an upper bound on ξ_i² = (g_{hiZZ}/g^SM_{HZZ})² · Γ^SM/(Γ^SM + Γ(h_i→ψ̄ψ)). The paper imposes ξ² < 0.1 as a conservative bound for m_hi = 90 GeV. It uses ξ² < 0.3 for 100 GeV, for later use. The ξ² definition includes the invisible h→ψ̄ψ decay width.\n\nWhich masses satisfy it: only m_ψ ≲ m_h1/2 (about 45 GeV) passes. There the invisible decay h1→ψ̄ψ is open and large, which suppresses ξ². For m_ψ > m_h1/2 that decay is closed, so ξ1² = cos²θ is always above 0.1 and LEP2 excludes the region.\n\nDirect detection: the LEP2-allowed region (orange points) of the m_h1 = 90 GeV, m_h2 = 500 GeV set is entirely excluded by the CDMS and Xenon bounds of that time.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "0803.2932v2", "section_id": "3"}, {"arxiv_id": "0803.2932v2", "section_id": "4"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261117T082739Z_eval-12_staged_ed5a", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "LEP2 condition: for the Higgs-strahlung process e+e- → Z h, the SM 114.4 GeV bound is recast as an upper bound on ξ_i² = (g_{hiZZ}/g^SM_{HZZ})² · Γ^SM/(Γ^SM + Γ(h_i→ψ̄ψ)). The paper imposes ξ² < 0.1 as a conservative bound for m_hi = 90 GeV. It uses ξ² < 0.3 for 100 GeV, for later use. The ξ² definition includes the invisible h→ψ̄ψ decay width.\n\nWhich masses satisfy it: only m_ψ ≲ m_h1/2 (about 45 GeV) passes. There the invisible decay h1→ψ̄ψ is open and large, which suppresses ξ². For m_ψ > m_h1/2 that decay is closed, so ξ1² = cos²θ is always above 0.1 and LEP2 excludes the region.\n\nDirect detection: the LEP2-allowed region (orange points) of the m_h1 = 90 GeV, m_h2 = 500 GeV set is entirely excluded by the CDMS and Xenon bounds of that time.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "0803.2932v2", "section_id": "3"}, {"arxiv_id": "0803.2932v2", "section_id": "4"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 9.818, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 17063, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 883, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11203, "cache_read_input_tokens": 7935, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-17T08:27:49+00:00"}
